  <data name="Zshot_ColorManagementDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Reads the monitor's ICC profile to parse the real color gamut and writes the cICP/ICC chunk into the file. HDR is always BT2020; for SDR, on = real gamut from ICC, off = BT709. Enabling first probes the monitor; if the color config is invalid (e.g. VM, missing ICC), it cannot be turned on.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Zshot_ColorManagementUnavailable" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The monitor's color configuration is invalid (common on VMs or devices without an ICC profile). Color management cannot be enabled.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Zshot_AutoConvertSDRDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>HDR screenshots also save an SDR copy (Ultra HDR JPEG).</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Zshot_DeleteHDRIfSDR" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Delete HDR if SDR Content</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Zshot_DeleteHDRIfSDRDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>When an HDR-format frame is actually SDR content (maxCLL below threshold), automatically convert to SDR and delete the HDR file. The format follows the SDR storage format.</value>
  </data>
